 "side": "Light",
 "description": "Sits like a fat 'ol duck.",
 "strategy": "Just something you really haven’t seen before- a podracing QMC. I was trying to think of a deck that could really take advantage of I Did It!, and QMC seemed to be the best choice. Otherwise, run it like a normal QMC, flip on turn 2 or 3, and take near squat damage. Combine that with retrieval, and you’re pretty set. Just slooowly drain the opponent out, coupled with the occasional beatdown. You can actually take fairly decent advantage of Civil Disorder (V)- although I would like to add a Senator Palpatine to screw Senate up. Any ideas on how to do that? Also, I’m worried about my lack of Controls. Any ideas? I also want to add STRans (V).\n\nMatchups:\n\nDark Deal: Fight for space hard- or you’ll lose it.\n\nMKOS: They shouldn’t be able to outdamage you. And if they try to come fight you on Cloud City, let them.\n\nHunt Down: Choose your battles wisely.\n\nCCT: Killeet Han and Lando.\n\nROps: He probably won't come to you, and it will be hard for you to go to him, so just enjoy the quiet life on CC.\n\nBHBM: Avoid beats. Give him Luke if he wants it.\n\nAOBS: Keep Luke safe. Protect Luke.\n\nWatto: Spend 8 to use Watto, then TBS the deck.\n\nCombat: If you must Combat, track.\n\nOther things- do your thing.",
